format: 2
name: a packageless user record named like a ledger hash type
class: Probe
method: m
arg: 420102
expect: REJECT JULC0100
note: ADR-067 D9: rejected with JULC0081 in M3b. Baseline as found in M0: TypeResolver resolves ledger hash names by simple name. A subset rule: a type does not take a name read as a type of JuLC's.
---
import java.math.BigInteger;
record PubKeyHash(byte[] h) {}

public class Probe {

    public static byte[] m(byte[] h) {
        PubKeyHash p = new PubKeyHash(h);
        return p.h();
    }
}
